---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Solar Racking and Mounting Thailand | Roof Mount Systems | JJ Com Solar Cell';
const description = 'Professional solar racking and mounting installation in Thailand. Corrosion-resistant aluminium mounting systems for concrete, metal, and tile roofs. Engineered for tropical storms and high winds. Free quote.';
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="website"
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Solar Racking and Mounting Installation",
    "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "areaServed": { "@type": "Country", "name": "Thailand" }
  }}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Services</span> / <span>Racking and Mounting</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-yellow/20 text-solar-yellow px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6">
        Serving Thailand Since 2016
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Solar Racking and Mounting Systems</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Corrosion-resistant aluminium mounting systems engineered for Thailand's tropical climate, monsoon winds, and diverse roof types.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">25yr</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Structural warranty</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">150+</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">km/h wind rated</div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green mb-2">100%</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Aluminium construction</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Solar Racking Systems Work</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        A solar racking system is the structural foundation that holds photovoltaic modules in place for 25 years or more. It must withstand tropical storms, seismic events, thermal expansion, and constant UV exposure -- all while keeping panels at the optimal tilt angle to maximise annual energy yield.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        The mounting system consists of several integrated components: roof attachments that penetrate or clamp to the existing roof structure; rails that span across the roof surface; and module clamps that grip the aluminium frame of each solar panel. Every connection point must be electrically bonded and grounded to prevent galvanic corrosion between dissimilar metals and to provide a safe path for lightning strikes.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        In Thailand, we engineer mounting systems for a design wind speed of 150 kilometres per hour -- matching the maximum wind loads specified in Thai building codes for coastal and exposed areas. This exceeds typical monsoon wind speeds but provides the safety margin needed when storms occasionally intensify beyond forecast levels. All structural bolts use A2-70 stainless steel to resist corrosion from salt spray and acid rain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Mounting Solutions by Roof Type</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Concrete and Flat Roofs</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The most common roof type in modern Thai construction. We use chemical anchor bolts drilled into structural concrete with epoxy resin bonding. For large commercial installations, we install aluminium ballasted frames that distribute weight across the roof slab without penetrations -- ideal where waterproofing integrity must be preserved. Tilt angles are optimised based on latitude; for most of Thailand (12°N to 18°N), we set panels between 10 and 15 degrees for optimal year-round production.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Metal Sheet Roofs (Trapezoidal)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Common in factories, warehouses, and rural homes. We use standing-seam clamps or L-foot brackets with butyl rubber flashings that create a watertight seal around each penetration point. Thermal expansion clips allow the metal roof to expand and contract without stressing the mounting rails. Critical for Thailand where metal roofs reach 60°C in direct sun, creating significant thermal movement cycles daily.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-2">Ceramic Tile Roofs</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Traditional Thai architecture often uses curved ceramic tiles. Installation requires removing individual tiles, installing flashing plates beneath, and replacing tiles around the mounting points. We use tile hooks designed for the specific tile profile -- S-tiles, W-tiles, or flat interlocking tiles. Extra care is taken to maintain the roof's water-shedding capability, as broken or improperly seated tiles lead to leaks during monsoon rains.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why Proper Mounting Matters in Thailand</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Thailand's climate is uniquely challenging for solar mounting systems. Year-round high humidity accelerates corrosion of steel components, which is why we specify marine-grade anodised aluminium (6063-T5 alloy) for all rails, clamps, and brackets. This alloy forms a protective oxide layer that prevents further corrosion even when scratched or abraded.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Coastal installations face additional salt spray exposure. On Koh Chang and similar islands, airborne salt deposits on metal surfaces within weeks, creating electrolytic cells that pit and weaken structural members. Our mounting hardware receives additional anodising thickness (20 microns versus the standard 10) and all fasteners are A4-80 marine stainless steel -- the highest corrosion resistance class available.
        </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Thermal expansion is significant. A 6-meter aluminium rail on a Thai rooftop can expand by 8 to 10 millimetres between dawn (25°C) and peak afternoon (65°C). Our systems use slotted rail joints and expansion clips that accommodate this movement without stressing panel frames or loosening connections over time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What You Get with Our Racking Service</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Structural survey:</strong> We assess roof condition, load-bearing capacity, orientation, and shading before recommending a mounting approach.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Engineering design:</strong> Tilt angle, row spacing, and wind load calculations prepared for your specific location and roof type.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Quality components:</strong> Rails, clamps, brackets, and fasteners from Tier 1 manufacturers with 25-year structural warranties.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Waterproofing guarantee:</strong> All roof penetrations sealed with EPDM rubber flashings and polyurethane sealant. We warranty against leaks for 5 years.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Electrical grounding:</strong> Complete bonding and earthing system connecting all rails, frames, and inverters to your building's earth electrode.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-solar-green text-xl">✓</span> <span class="text-gray-700"><strong>Inspection and certification:</strong> Post-installation torque check on all fasteners, alignment verification, and structural load test. Certificate of compliance provided.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Mounting System Specifications</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Wind Load Rating</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Engineered for 150 km/h sustained winds with gusts to 200 km/h. Exceeds Thai Building Code requirements for all regions except direct cyclone zones.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Snow Load (Northern Thailand)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Systems for Chiang Mai and mountainous regions rated to 50 kg/m² snow load -- far above any historical accumulation in Thailand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Seismic Rating</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Ballasted systems and flexible joint designs accommodate ground movement without panel displacement or connection failure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Tilt Angle Optimisation</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">10-15° for Southern/Central Thailand. 15-20° for Northern regions. Steeper angles shed dust and debris more effectively in dry season.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/services/solar-panel-installation" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Solar Panel Installation</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Complete system design including racking, panels, and inverters</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Calculate how many panels fit your available roof space</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Need a Mounting Assessment?</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Get a free structural survey and mounting system recommendation for your roof type.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Get a Free Quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
